Requirements: 12   with obligations: 12

[task-01] For a named plausible defect, the review builds the smallest edit that makes
    that defect true, applies it to a throwaway copy of the code, and runs the project's
    candidate tests against the altered copy. A test that fails is shown to discriminate
    for that defect. When no test fails, the candidate tests are shown not to
    discriminate for it. Either way the conclusion is an observation rather than a
    prediction, and is recorded at the strongest evidence tier the review produces on
    its own.
    -> smallest-edit-that-makes-defect-true  [functional/explicit]
       The review builds the smallest edit that makes the named plausible defect true.
    -> run-candidate-tests-on-altered-copy  [functional/explicit]
       Run the project's candidate tests against the altered copy.
    -> test-fails-discriminate-defect  [functional/explicit]
       A test that fails is shown to discriminate for that defect.
    -> candidate-tests-not-discriminate-when-none-fail  [functional/explicit]
       When no test fails, the candidate tests are shown not to discriminate for the
       defect.
    -> observation-not-prediction  [invariant/explicit]
       The conclusion is an observation rather than a prediction.
    -> recorded-at-strongest-evidence-tier  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The conclusion is recorded at the strongest evidence tier the review produces on
       its own.

[task-02] The injected text is recorded next to the result, so a reader who disagrees
    with what was injected can see exactly what it was.
    -> injected-text-recorded-next-to-result  [functional/explicit]
       The injected text is recorded next to the result.

[task-03] Before anything is altered, the candidate tests run once against the code as
    delivered. A test that already fails there tells nothing when it fails later, so
    this run is what makes the later result mean anything. If any candidate test fails
    on the delivered code, the review stops and says why. A project can be configured to
    continue anyway, for a failure its owners have chosen to live with; then the failing
    tests take no part in any conclusion, and the report says which ones were set aside.
    -> candidate-tests-run-once-before-changes  [functional/explicit]
       Before any changes are made, the candidate tests are run once against the code as
       delivered.
    -> stop-review-on-failing-candidate-test  [functional/explicit]
       If any candidate test fails on the delivered code, the review stops and says why.
    -> continue-with-set-aside-tests  [functional/explicit]
       When the project is configured to continue anyway after a failing candidate test,
       the failing tests are set aside and take no part in any conclusion.
    -> report-lists-set-aside-tests  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The report states which failing tests were set aside.

[task-04] The existing judgement that reads code without running it does not go away,
    and does not run first. It runs on what execution could not settle: a defect no edit
    could express, a defect whose edit could not be built, and every defect at all when
    the code cannot be run. Where nothing can be run, the review reaches the conclusions
    it reaches today and its evidence stays at the weaker tier.
    -> preserve-code-reading-judgement  [compatibility/explicit]
       The existing judgement that reads code without running it does not go away.
    -> does-not-run-first  [invariant/explicit]
       The code-reading judgement does not run before execution-based review; it remains
       a later-stage review rather than the first pass.
    -> execution-could-not-settle-defects  [functional/explicit]
       The judgement that reads code without running it runs on what execution could not
       settle: defects no edit could express, defects whose edit could not be built, and
       every defect at all when the code cannot be run.
    -> preserve-current-review-conclusions-when-unrunnable  [invariant/explicit]
       Where nothing can be run, the review reaches the conclusions it reaches today.
    -> weaker-tier-evidence  [invariant/explicit]
       The evidence for this judgement stays at the weaker tier.

[task-05] A defect execution did not settle carries the reason it did not.
    -> carry-reason-for-non-settlement  [invariant/explicit]
       A defect execution that did not settle carries the reason it did not.

[constraint-01] The edit replaces one continuous stretch of a single file, within a
    region the defect names. A defect naming no region cannot be edited, and says so.
    -> single-continuous-edit-in-named-region  [functional/explicit]
       The edit replaces one continuous stretch of a single file within the region named
       by the defect.
    -> no-edit-without-named-region  [invariant/explicit]
       A defect that names no region is not editable and is reported as such.

[constraint-02] A file that has a parser must still parse after the edit. A file with no
    parser is not invalid for lacking one — a requirement can be stated in prose and
    broken in prose, and the tests that read that prose are the ones that catch it.
    -> parser-files-still-parse  [invariant/explicit]
       A file that has a parser still parses after the edit.
    -> no-parser-not-invalid  [invariant/explicit]
       A file with no parser is not invalid for lacking one.

[constraint-03] Whether an edit is valid is settled by mechanical checks alone.
    -> mechanical-validity-checks  [invariant/explicit]
       Whether an edit is valid is settled by mechanical checks alone.

[exclusion-01] Deciding whether a project's tests can be run at all, and which of them
    are candidates.
    -> tests-candidate-selection  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter how the review decides whether a project's tests can be
       run at all or which tests are candidates.

[exclusion-02] Recording which lines of code a test executed.
    -> no-line-execution-recording  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not record which lines of code a test executed.

[exclusion-03] Writing or altering a test so that a defect can be reached.
    -> no-test-writing-or-altering-for-defect-reachability  [test_demand/explicit]
       The change does not include writing or altering a test so that a defect can be
       reached.

[exclusion-04] Running the project's whole test suite.
    -> no-whole-suite-run  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not run the project's whole test suite.

